15 0 obj
<< /A 46 0 R /Alt (Flowchart depicting the process of farms' participation in a survey. Out of 196 identified farms, 38 were reached by phone, and 158 were initially unavailable. During the survey, 18 additional farms were referred, totaling 56 enrolled farms. All 56 were included in the analysis, with 26 included and 30 excluded from mortality analysis.) /K 0 /P 8 0 R /Pg 34 0 R /S /Figure /T () >>
endobj
16 0 obj
<< /A 47 0 R /Alt (Bar chart showing the percentage of farms based on communication frequency. \215Can't tell\216 is highest at 27.0%, followed by \215Seasonal\216 at 19.5%. Others: \215Quarterly\216 and \215Throughout the year\216 at 12.7%, \215Monthly\216 at 10.8%, \215Twice a year\216 at 10.6%, \215Once a year\216 at 6.8%. Y-axis: Percentage of farms, X-axis: Frequency categories.) /K 0 /P 8 0 R /Pg 35 0 R /S /Figure /T () >>
endobj
17 0 obj
<< /A 48 0 R /Alt (Horizontal bar chart displaying percentages of different causes. Streptococcus agalactiae and ISKNV each account for 32%. Unknown causes are at 24%. Aeromonas spp contributes 9%, and Fungi account for 3%.) /K 0 /P 8 0 R /Pg 36 0 R /S /Figure /T () >>
endobj
18 0 obj
<< /A 49 0 R /Alt (Map depicting the percentage of farms affected in five regions: Afadzato South \(84% affected\), Asuogyaman \(38%\), Lower Manya Krobo \(22%\), Shai Osudoku \(0%\), and South Tongu \(50%\). Regions are color-coded by the percentage scale, from yellow \(high\) to purple \(low\). A legend indicates affected and unaffected farms, with pie charts on each region showing affected proportions.) /K 1 /P 8 0 R /Pg 36 0 R /S /Figure /T () >>
endobj
19 0 obj
<< /A 50 0 R /Alt (Map depicting percentages of farms affected by a specific issue in five districts. Afadzato South shows 74% affected, colored orange. Asuogyaman and South Tongu each show 50% affected, colored pink. Lower Manya-Krobo shows 11% affected, colored light blue. Shai Osudoku shows 20% affected, colored purple. A color gradient represents affected percentages, from yellow for 100% to purple for 0%. Gray circles indicate affected and unaffected farms.) /K 0 /P 8 0 R /Pg 37 0 R /S /Figure /T () >>
endobj
20 0 obj
<< /A 51 0 R /Alt (Bar chart showing the response of farms regarding disease factors: inadequate biosecurity, poor water quality, seasonal variation, poor handling, and high stocking density. Responses are categorized as Yes \(blue\), No \(red\), and Missing \(gray\). Inadequate biosecurity and seasonal variation have the highest \215Yes\216 responses.) /K 1 /P 8 0 R /Pg 37 0 R /S /Figure /T () >>
endobj
21 0 obj
<< /A 52 0 R /Alt (Bar charts comparing diagnostic methods used by farms in different regions: Afadjato South, Asuogyaman, Lower Manya Krobo, Shai Osudoku, and South Tong. Methods include: using clinical signs, taking samples to labs, consulting other farmers, and calling extension officers. Bars are color-coded by response: orange for \215No,\216 blue for \215Yes,\216 with percentages labeled on the x-axis.) /K 0 /P 8 0 R /Pg 38 0 R /S /Figure /T () >>
endobj
22 0 obj
<< /A 53 0 R /Alt (Violin plots display education level distributions for \215Strep\216 \(panel A\) and \215ISKNV\216 \(panel B\) with \215Absent,\216 \215Present,\216 and \215NA\216 categories. Panel A has a Wilcoxon p-value of 0.0923, while panel B is 0.0139. Each plot shows variation in education levels with distinct shapes for categories.) /K 0 /P 8 0 R /Pg 39 0 R /S /Figure /T () >>
endobj
23 0 obj
<< /A 54 0 R /Alt (Two graphs labeled A and B illustrate the effect of poor handling. Graph A shows a blue bar with a log-odds estimate around three, showing statistical significance with p = 0.0011672. Below, a line graph displays predicted probabilities of \215Strep\216 increasing from 0.25 to 0.75. Graph B has a similar layout with a log-odds estimate of three and p = 0.0062372. The line graph shows predicted probabilities of \215SKINV\216 rising from 0.25 to 0.75. Error bars are present in both graphs.) /K 1 /P 8 0 R /Pg 39 0 R /S /Figure /T () >>
endobj
24 0 obj
<< /A 55 0 R /Alt (Heatmap titled \215Disease Signs by District \(proportion of farms\)\216 displaying various disease signs across five districts: Afadjato South, Asuogyaman, Lower Manya Krobo, Shai Osudoku, and South Tong. Color gradient indicates prevalence, with red for higher and green for lower proportions. Disease signs include exophthalmia, swollen abdomen, skin lesions, poor growth rates, skin hemorrhages, fin rot, stationary at one place, abnormal swimming, change in skin color, cloudy eye, pale gills, and inflammation of internal organs.) /K 0 /P 8 0 R /Pg 40 0 R /S /Figure /T () >>
endobj
